{"role":"assistant","content":"I can see the problem clearly: `bot.py:130-133` puts the static `INSTRUCTIONS` and the volatile athlete context (date, profile, facts) in a single `cache_control` block. The log confirms it — e.g. line 5: after a `save_fact`, round 2 pays `cache_creation_input_tokens: 1061` with `cache_read_input_tokens: 0`, re-caching the whole prompt including instructions that never change.\n\nLet me check the data file and git state before editing.","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"tool_noC7mHruOaPntroMnmZc1Sco","function":{"name":"Read","arguments":"{\"path\":\"data/athletes.json\"}"}},{"type":"function","id":"tool_E1JTn1JNjjMP48XWjBds3dZN","function":{"name":"Bash","arguments":"{\"command\":\"git status --short && git log --oneline -5\"}"}}]}
