{"role":"assistant","content":"Now I'll verify the fix end-to-end without touching the external API: `reply()` accepts an injected `llm`, so I'll run the real tool loop with a fake LLM that emits a `save_fact` on round 1 and text on round 2, and assert the request structure. I'll back up the data and log files first since the run writes to them, and restore after.","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"tool_fymny5bzFqe1kJAkEqhgll78","function":{"name":"Bash","arguments":"{\"command\":\"cp data/athletes.json data/athletes.json.bak && cp logs/usage.jsonl logs/usage.jsonl.bak && python3 - <<'EOF'\\nimport sys\\nsys.path.insert(0, \\\".\\\")\\nimport bot\\nfrom bot import reply, INSTRUCTIONS, load_athlete\\n\\ncalls = []\\n\\nclass Block:\\n    def __init__(self, **kw):\\n        self.__dict__.update(kw)\\n    def model_dump(self):\\n        return dict(self.__dict__)\\n\\nclass Usage:\\n    input_tokens = 10\\n    cache_creation_input_tokens = 0\\n    cache_read_input_tokens = 0\\n    output_tokens = 5\\n\\nclass Resp:\\n    def __init__(self, content, stop_reason):\\n        self.content = content\\n        self.stop_reason = stop_reason\\n        self.usage = Usage()\\n\\nclass FakeLLM:\\n    def __init__(self):\\n        self.n = 0\\n    def create(self, **kw):\\n        calls.append(kw)\\n        self.n += 1\\n        if self.n == 1:\\n            return Resp([Block(type=\\\"tool_use\\\", id=\\\"tu_1\\\", name=\\\"save_fact\\\",\\n                               input={\\\"fact\\\": \\\"Bought a wind trainer\\\"})], \\\"tool_use\\\")\\n        return Resp([Block(type=\\\"text\\\", text=\\\"Noted. Anything else?\\\")], \\\"end_turn\\\")\\n\\nout = reply(\\\"42\\\", \\\"I just bought a wind trainer\\\", llm=FakeLLM())\\nprint(\\\"bot reply:\\\", out)\\nassert len(calls) == 2, f\\\"expected 2 rounds, got {len(calls)}\\\"\\n\\nfor i, kw in enumerate(calls, 1):\\n    sys_prompt = kw[\\\"system\\\"]\\n    assert isinstance(sys_prompt, list) and len(sys_prompt) == 2, f\\\"round {i}: system must be two blocks\\\"\\n    for b in sys_prompt:\\n        assert b.get(\\\"cache_control\\\") == {\\\"type\\\": \\\"ephemeral\\\"}, f\\\"round {i}: a block is missing its cache_control marker\\\"\\n    assert sys_prompt[0][\\\"text\\\"] == INSTRUCTIONS, f\\\"round {i}: block 0 must be exactly INSTRUCTIONS\\\"\\n\\nassert calls[0][\\\"system\\\"][0][\\\"text\\\"] == calls[1][\\\"system\\\"][0][\\\"text\\\"], \\\"static block changed across a memory write\\\"\\n\\ntail1 = calls[0][\\\"system\\\"][1][\\\"text\\\"]\\ntail2 = calls[1][\\\"system\\\"][1][\\\"text\\\"]\\nassert \\\"Bought a wind trainer\\\" in tail2, \\\"new fact missing from tail after save_fact\\\"\\nassert tail1 != tail2, \\\"tail should change after save_fact\\\"\\nassert tail2.count(\\\"\\\\n\\\") - tail1.count(\\\"\\\\n\\\") == 1, \\\"tail should grow by exactly one fact line\\\"\\n\\nassert calls[0][\\\"tools\\\"] == calls[1][\\\"tools\\\"], \\\"tools changed within one message's loop\\\"\\n\\nfor f in load_athlete(\\\"42\\\").facts:\\n    assert f in tail2, f\\\"fact missing from tail: {f}\\\"\\n\\nprint(\\\"--- tail before save_fact ---\\\"); print(tail1)\\nprint(\\\"--- tail after save_fact ---\\\");  print(tail2)\\nprint(\\\"ALL CHECKS PASSED\\\")\\nEOF\\nrc=$?; mv data/athletes.json.bak data/athletes.json && mv logs/usage.jsonl.bak logs/usage.jsonl; exit $rc\"}"}}]}
